        "title": "policy: repair denied gateway http endpoints",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Restack on current `main` after #99720 merged.\n- Classify `policy/gateway-http-endpoint-enabled` as an automatic narrowing repair.\n- Wire `doctor --fix` to set the exact reported denied Gateway HTTP endpoint `enabled` paths to `false`.\n- Leave URL-fetch allowlist findings manual; this PR only disables denied endpoints and preserves nested endpoint config.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\n`doctor --fix` can now repair denied Gateway HTTP endpoint findings by disabling the reported endpoint paths while preserving nested endpoint options such as URL-fetch settings.\n\nReal environment tested:\nWindows PowerShell in `C:\\src\\openclaw-policy-gateway-http-push`, source checkout at PR head `1fcd3219f46a81938a91df78856136e30753dbfdb`, based on `upstream/main` `82106a18b3beaaff085ca3258a6f09cd19348d03` after #99720 merged.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD`\n2. `git diff --stat HEAD~1..HEAD`\n3. `git diff --name-status HEAD~1..HEAD`\n\nEvidence after fix:\n`git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` exited 0. The final PR diff is the intended five-file slice: `extensions/policy/src/doctor/automatic-repairs.ts`, `fix-metadata.ts`, `metadata.test.ts`, `register.test.ts`, and `scopes/gateway.ts`, with 70 insertions and 2 deletions. The new focused test `repairs denied gateway HTTP endpoint findings` covers disabling `chatCompletions` and `responses`, verifies both repair change messages, checks no remaining findings, and verifies nested URL-fetch config remains intact.\n\nObserved result after fix:\nThe repair path uses `setFindingConfigValues(..., \"enabled\", false)` for `policy/gateway-http-endpoint-enabled`, so only the reported endpoint `enabled` fields are narrowed. The PR no longer carries the already-merged channel-ingress commits from #99720.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nThis clean push worktree has no `node_modules`, so I did not rerun Vitest locally after the final post-#99720 restack. GitHub CI is running on the pushed PR head.\n\n## Stack\n\n- Now directly stacked on `main` after #99720 merged.\n- Next downstream slice remains #99776 after this PR is ready.",
